35,2,1,talk,George,,It seems that strict monitoring and constant requests for favors are what truly damage these relationships.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The diary shows a significant imbalance in usage hours, especially during holidays and weekends.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The car is often neglected. Short trips are damaging it, and it's frequently left in a poor state for the next person.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The fixed costs are higher than I thought, and the fuel contributions are very uneven.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I saw the fuel receipts. Some people pay much more than others. It's not very fair, is it?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,George,,"@Minato, fairness isn't just about money. If we focus only on receipts, we might create more tension.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, I agree. The recurring weekly trips are the main source of scheduling conflicts and stress.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, the schedule is one thing, but the physical state of the car is another. We can't ignore the wear and tear.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If we want an even split, we have to account for both the fixed costs and the actual fuel usage.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I just want us to be honest about who drives the most. That way, we can decide together.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,George,,We should avoid a system where we are constantly checking each other's figures. It leads to resentment.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,A fixed schedule for the recurring trips would reduce the time spent negotiating every single evening.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I believe we need a rule about the state of the car upon return. It shouldn't be a gamble every morning.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,A simple split of fixed costs and a usage-based fuel payment seems the most logical approach.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,I think we should use the real numbers we found to make a plan. I don't want anyone to feel sad.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,George,,Let's ensure the solution doesn't make us feel like we are policing each other.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Efficiency is key. Reducing the administrative burden is as important as the financial split.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I will support any option that ensures the car is ready and reliable for the next user.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Let's look for a balance between strict fairness and ease of management.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I hope we can all agree on something that makes everyone happy.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
